      "archaeologicalRemains": "notvisible",
      "details": "<p><span>The imagery location of E\u0161asurra\u00a0is based on\u00a0</span><a href=\"https://uppsala.app.box.com/s/cgm386mr39f0we39y8v49ktecc664k0k/file/722112939158\">Peders\u00e9n 2021 fig. 2.2</a><span>, which shows a plan of eastern Babylon, with 200 m UTM coordinates given.\u00a0 The site of the temple of the god I\u0161hara is known since it was excavated in 1901\u201302. The remains of the building are no longer visible; they are just below the surface. The ruins of this 1710 m\u00b2 temple are located approximately at\u00a0</span>32.530856, 44.424226.</p>",
